    "result_text": "`check_super_user` now exists in `lnbits/decorators.py`. The admin endpoints that should be super-user-only already use it, so I didn't change them. I haven't run the code or the tests. The one command I tried, a Python import check, needed approval and didn't run.\n\n- **What was wrong:** `check_super_user` was imported in `lnbits/__init__.py`, `admin_api.py`, `user_api.py` and `node_api.py`, but it was never defined. Those imports would have failed.\n- **What I added:** it follows the catalog pattern `auth.check_admin@v1`. It returns 403 if the account is not an admin or has no password set. It also returns 403 if the account is not the super user. The `# pcat:` marker is above the function.\n- **Where it's used:** `admin_api.py` already applies it to `DELETE /settings`, `GET /restart` and `GET /backup`. I left the other admin endpoints (audit, monitor, testemail, settings get/update) on `check_admin`. Making them super-user-only would lock regular admins out of them. Say so if you want that.\n- **Catalog check:** `check_code` reports no high-severity deviations. The only finding is a low-severity note about the added super-user check, and no `pcat-allow` approval is needed."
